6. Build tools — KAGE engine (GPL-3.0) and Potrace (GPL-2.0+)
========================================================================
The Chinese hanzi were produced by rendering GlyphWiki's freely-licensed
skeleton data (section 2) into outlines with the KAGE engine
(https://github.com/MihailJP/kage-engine, GNU GPL v3) and then tracing the
result with Potrace (https://potrace.sourceforge.net/, GNU GPL v2+).

These are BUILD TOOLS. None of their program code is contained in or
distributed with the font files; the font stores only the resulting glyph
outlines, which are derived from the free GlyphWiki data, not from the tools'
source code. On this basis this font is distributed under the permissive terms
above (sections 1-5) rather than the GPL. This is the same position taken by
HZ Socho itself, which is likewise generated by the KAGE engine and Potrace
from GlyphWiki data yet released under the X11 terms above by the very author
of this KAGE-engine fork. (Potrace additionally states that its tracing output
is not a derivative work of Potrace.)

Note: this is a good-faith reading of the upstream terms, not legal advice.
If you redistribute the *build scripts* together with a copy of the KAGE
engine or Potrace, keep those tools under their own GPL licenses.

